  },
  "definitions": {
    "hit": "a call whose key is already in the policy's run-scope cache; the memo's value is returned and the tool does not run",
    "cacheable_call": "a call the policy admits to its cache: every call for P1-P3, reads only for P4 (writes and control tools are refused before the lookup). Hit rate is hits / cacheable calls.",
    "writes_served": "an unsafe hit where the call is a write: the mutation is answered from a memo and never runs, while the agent's belief that it ran is unchanged",
    "stale_read": "an unsafe hit where the call is a read and some write that executed names an entity id the read names, at a position strictly between the memo's store position and the hit; the memo predates the write",
    "cross_tenant": "an unsafe hit where the call is a read, the memo was stored under a different known tenant, and the hit is not already stale; tenant is the single user_id named by the record, and an unknown tenant on either side is never counted. The class is defined by provenance, not by demonstrated damage: a cache cannot tell a tenant-agnostic catalog read (a product row, a flight search) from a tenant-scoped one, so both are counted; unsafe_by_tool.cross_tenant shows how much of the class is catalog traffic",
    "unsafe_hit": "the union of writes_served, stale_reads and cross_tenant, each hit assigned to exactly one class by the precedence writes_served > stale_reads > cross_tenant, so the breakdown sums to the total; unsafe_by_class_overlapping reports the pre-precedence counts where a hit can be in more than one class",
    "control_hits": "hits on control tools (think, transfer_to_human_agents). They are memoised by P1-P3 and refused by P4, but they are not one of the three defined unsafe classes and are reported separately rather than counted in unsafe_hits",
    "tenant": "the single distinct user_id named by a record's calls, else unknown. Cross-tenant counts are a lower bound: 49 of 325 records name no user_id and one names two",
    "hit_rate": "hits / cacheable_calls, rounded to 4 decimals; hit_rate_of_all_calls uses every replayed call as the denominator and is given so the four policies can be compared on one base",
    "not_counted": "reads naming no entity id (list_all_*, search_*, calculate) cannot be joined to a write; unknown tenants cannot be compared; a failed write is indistinguishable from a landed one in this corpus, so every replayed write is treated as having landed"
  },
